# Docs & commit language

Describe spring-a2ui in **our** product terms. Chat may use shortcuts for context; repo docs, ADRs, plans, READMEs, changelogs, and commit messages should not.

## Prefer

| Intent | Language |
|--------|----------|
| What we are | Spring GenUI backend **runtime** for OSS product builders |
| What builders keep | Their design system and frontend |
| What we own | Compose → validate → stream → fail-fast → actions |
| Genre | In-product surfaces: process **steps** and page **slots** (not chat identity, not verticals like OPS/HITL) |
| Optional later interop | Foreign-client bridge / optional interop adapter (demand-gated) |
| What we are not | Chat product shell; foreign interaction protocol as core identity; their datastore; a hosted platform |

## Accurate protocol / stack names are fine

A2UI, A2A, ADK, MCP, Spring, Spring AI — when we actually integrate with or implement them.

## Generic terms are fine

Third-party chat clients, agent↔app pipes, FE shells.

## Avoid as identity

**Platform** as the noun on the box. Keep it only as a negation (we are not a platform datastore / memory / outbox).
**Island** for a page placement — use **slot**. Spec *slot values* (`title`, `body`) are a different word; say **slot values** when you mean the template fill map.
